        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 25 at 3:33PM MDT by NWS Denver CO</headline>
        <description>At 333 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a line of showers extending
from over Littleton to 5 miles north of Bennett, or extending from 10
miles southwest of Denver to 28 miles east of Denver, moving north at
15 mph.

HAZARD...Landspouts and wind gusts up to 40 mph.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Minor damage to outdoor objects is possible. Gusty winds
could knock down tree limbs and blow around unsecured
objects.

Locations impacted include...
Aurora, Centennial, Highlands Ranch, Littleton, southern Englewood,
Greenwood Village, Lone Tree, Bennett, Arapahoe Park, Buckley SFB,
Watkins, Manila Village, Cherry Hills Village, Foxfield and Cherry
Creek Reservoir.
</description>
        <instruction>Monitor the weather situation closely and be alert for threatening
weather conditions.</instruction>
